<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλολῡγ-ών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όνος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>croaking of the male frog,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				536a11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				9.13
			</span></i> ; <i>note of water-creatures,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.139
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				948
			</span></i>, an unknown <i>animal,</i> evidently named from its note :
			some take it for <i>a small owl,</i> others for a <i>singing
				bird,</i> others again for the <i>tree-frog ;</i> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				104
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.291.5
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
